    "text": "<math> <mrow>  <msup>   <mrow>    <mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\">     <mrow>      <mtext>Pt</mtext><msub>       <mrow>        <mfenced>         <mrow>          <msub>           <mrow>            <mtext>NH</mtext></mrow>           <mtext>3</mtext>          </msub>          </mrow>        </mfenced></mrow>       <mtext>4</mtext>      </msub>      <msub>       <mrow>        <mtext>Cl</mtext></mrow>       <mtext>2</mtext>      </msub>      </mrow>    </mfenced></mrow>   <mrow>    <mtext>2+</mtext></mrow>  </msup>  </mrow></math> has <math> <mtext>2</mtext></math> geometrical isomers.<br /><br /><math> <mrow>  <msup>   <mrow>    <mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\">     <mrow>      <mtext>Pt</mtext><msub>       <mrow>        <mfenced>         <mrow>          <mtext>gly</mtext></mrow>        </mfenced></mrow>       <mtext>3</mtext>      </msub>      </mrow>    </mfenced></mrow>   <mrow>    <mtext>2</mtext><mo>&#x2212;</mo></mrow>  </msup>  </mrow></math> will have <math> <mn>2</mn></math> geometrical isomers, both of which will be optical active, giving a total of <math> <mn>4</mn></math> isomers.<br /><br /><math> <mrow>  <msup>   <mrow>    <mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\">     <mrow>      <mtext>Pt</mtext><msub>       <mrow>        <mfenced>         <mrow>          <mtext>en</mtext></mrow>        </mfenced></mrow>       <mtext>3</mtext>      </msub>      </mrow>    </mfenced></mrow>   <mrow>    <mtext>4+</mtext></mrow>  </msup>  </mrow></math> will have no geometrical isomers, but the compound will be optically active, hence total two isomers.<br /><br /><math> <mrow>  <mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\">   <mrow>    <mtext>Pt</mtext><msub>     <mrow>      <mfenced>       <mrow>        <msub>         <mrow>          <mtext>NH</mtext></mrow>         <mtext>3</mtext>        </msub>        </mrow>      </mfenced></mrow>     <mtext>2</mtext>    </msub>    <msub>     <mrow>      <mtext>Cl</mtext></mrow>     <mtext>2</mtext>    </msub>    </mrow>  </mfenced></mrow></math>